## 6. `ParitokConfig` and nested config dataclasses (`paritok/config.py`)

```python
@dataclass
class ParitokConfig:
    use_gpu_server: bool = False           # THE switch: False = self-host, True = paritok.com GPU
    compression:    CompressionConfig    = field(default_factory=CompressionConfig)
    history:        HistoryConfig        = field(default_factory=HistoryConfig)
    tool_discovery: ToolDiscoveryConfig  = field(default_factory=ToolDiscoveryConfig)
    local_model:    LocalModelConfig     = field(default_factory=LocalModelConfig)
    gpu_server:     GpuServerConfig      = field(default_factory=GpuServerConfig)
    trace:          TraceConfig          = field(default_factory=TraceConfig)
    codex:          CodexConfig          = field(default_factory=CodexConfig)
    shadow_storage: str = "memory"         # "memory" | "redis"

    @property
    def model(self) -> LocalModelConfig | GpuServerConfig:
        return self.gpu_server if self.use_gpu_server else self.local_model
```

Class methods:
```python
ParitokConfig.from_dict(data: dict) -> ParitokConfig
ParitokConfig.from_yaml(path: str | Path) -> ParitokConfig          # pyyaml safe_load
ParitokConfig.load(path: str | Path | None = None) -> ParitokConfig # file, then env overrides
```
`from_dict` raises `ValueError("Unknown config key '<k>' in <Type>. Valid: {...}")` on typos.

### `LocalModelConfig` — self-hosted (Ollama / any OpenAI-compatible endpoint)
| Field | Default |
|---|---|
| `base_url: str` | `"http://localhost:11434/v1"` |
| `model: str` | `"paritok-4b-v1"` |
| `temperature: float` | `0.0` |
| `timeout: float` | `120.0` |
| `api_key: str` | `""` (optional bearer; empty for local Ollama) |
| `num_ctx: int` | `8192` |

### `GpuServerConfig` — Paritok-hosted
| Field | Default |
|---|---|
| `base_url: str` | `"https://www.paritok.com/api"` |
| `model: str` | `"paritok-4b-v1"` |
| `temperature: float` | `0.0` |
| `timeout: float` | `90.0` |
| `api_key: str` | `""` (from paritok.com dashboard, or `PARITOK_API_KEY`) |

Docstring: the proxy POSTs each segment to `{base_url}/compress` and health-checks
`{base_url}/test`. If unreachable it **warns at startup and passes content through
uncompressed** (never aborts). Keys look like `pk_live_...` per the README.

### `CompressionConfig`
`min_tokens: int = 512`, `max_tokens: int = 50000`, `refusal_threshold: float = 0.05`.
Asserts: `min_tokens >= 0`, `max_tokens > min_tokens`, `0.0 <= refusal_threshold <= 1.0`.

### `HistoryConfig`
`enabled: bool = True`, `keep_recent_turns: int = 4`, `context_threshold: float = 0.8`,
`context_window: int = 200_000`. Asserts: `keep_recent_turns >= 1`,
`0 < context_threshold <= 1`, `context_window > 0`.

### `ToolDiscoveryConfig`
`strategy: str = "embedding"`, `top_k: int = 5`, `k_max: int = 8`, `adaptive: bool = True`,
`mcp_signal_threshold: float = 1.0`.
`_VALID_STRATEGIES = frozenset({"relevance", "passthrough", "embedding"})` (asserted).

### `TraceConfig`
`enabled: bool = False`, `path: str = "compress_trace.jsonl"`. When on, every compression
event (original + compressed body, tokens, ratio) is appended as JSONL. An env-var override
is read by `_resolve_trace_path(config)` and takes precedence — **UNVERIFIED** exact var name.

### `CodexConfig`
`enabled: bool = False`, `model: str = "gpt-5"`, `api_key: str = ""`, `config_path: str = ""`.
Codex ignores `OPENAI_BASE_URL`, so `paritok up`/`proxy` writes `~/.codex/config.toml`
(backing up any existing one) with `experimental_bearer_token`. Wire protocol fixed to
`responses`.

### Environment variables (all read in `ParitokConfig.load`)
| Var | Effect |
|---|---|
| `PARITOK_USE_GPU_SERVER` | truthy = `"1"`, `"true"`, `"yes"` (lowercased/stripped) -> `use_gpu_server` |
| `PARITOK_MODEL` | sets **both** `local_model.model` and `gpu_server.model` |
| `PARITOK_OLLAMA_URL` | sets `local_model.base_url` |
| `PARITOK_API_KEY` | sets **both** `gpu_server.api_key` and `local_model.api_key` |
| `PARITOK_DISABLE` | (read in `ParitokClient.__init__`) `"1"/"true"/"yes"` -> passthrough |

Env vars are applied **after** the YAML file, so they win.

